# Line endings are content here, not a checkout preference. rules/cs2demokit-rules.schema.json is
# compared byte-for-byte against the copy extracted from the CS2DemoKit package, which is written
# with LF, so a CRLF checkout fails ShippedSchemaDriftTests without anything having drifted. Pinning
# eol=lf keeps that gate honest on Windows. Mirrors the same fix upstream (CS2DemoKit #44).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never line-ending converted, never diffed as text. Git's heuristic would classify these
# correctly on its own; declaring them removes the question and stops a bad .gitattributes edit from
# ever corrupting a demo or a collision bake.
*.dem binary
*.tris binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary

# Shipped as-is to a shell that requires LF. Covered by the blanket rule above, but stated because a
# CRLF publish script fails at run time rather than at review time.
*.sh text eol=lf
